resources, implicit denies, and explicit denies) is recorded.\n  - Keep `deepcopy` of `{\"subject\": subject, \"roles\": list(roles), \"action\": action, \"resource\": resource, \"allowed\": decision.allowed, \"reason\": decision.reason}`.\n- `policy_engine.py`:\n  - `PolicyEngine.resolve_roles(roles)`:\n    - Track visited roles (`if name in resolved: continue`) before adding `name` to `resolved` and extending `pending` with `self.roles[name].parents`, so cycles terminate without losing any reachable roles.\n  - `PolicyEngine.decide(subject, roles, action, resource)`:\n    - Evaluate all `matching` rules:\n      - If any matching rule has `rule.effect == \"deny\"`, return `Decision(False, \"explicit_deny\")`.\n      - Else if any matching rule has `rule.effect == \"allow\"`, return `Decision(True, \"allow\")`.\n      - Else return `Decision(False, \"no_matching_allow\")`.\n    - Ensure `self.audit.record(subject, roles, action, resource, decision)` is called for every decision.\n\n### Verify Command\n- `python -m pytest -q --tb=short`\n","duration_seconds":14.1008263,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":30591,"output_tokens":1393,"thinking_tokens":142,"cache_read_tokens":46496,"total_tokens":31984}}}
